<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Bangla strings of the iPhone UI. values/strings.xml has the comments for each key: where the text shows,
  the placeholders and the length limits. docs/LOCALIZATION_GLOSSARY.md gives the terms and their sources.
  The polite form "আপনি" with "-উন", and English loanwords where Bangla iOS uses them ("সেভ", "ডিলিট", "এডিট").
  Bangla has the CLDR plural forms one and other; "one" also takes 0. A noun does not change after a number, so both forms are equal.
  The duration chips have no unit, because "12–24 ঘণ্টা" is longer than 7 characters: the captions name the hours.
-->
